{"calculus_ref":"stdo://releases/v2.5.1-rc.2/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md","clause_relations":[{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:refinement-construction-availability","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:result-algebra","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:target"},{"literal":"candidate_ready -> satisfied; refused -> falsified; incomplete -> indeterminate; re_entry_requested -> out_of_frame or invalid_basis.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:refinements-map-totally-to-core","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"relation","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:maps-to","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:construction-availability-maps-to-core"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:diagnostic-order","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"Diagnosis asks, in this order: 1 Was the correct declared frame activated? 2 Were the subject and basis exact? 3 Was the actor inside the capability envelope? 4 Was admissible evidence available? 5 Is a material variable or invariant missing from the frame? 6 Is a required conjunction or translation missing? 7 Is the evaluation family itself wrong or incomplete? 8 Is another frame required? The order prevents every difficult evaluation from creating another frame.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"P2","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:diagnostic-order-is-eight-questions-in-order"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:refinement-disposition","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:result-algebra","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"accept, local_repair, re_enter and reject are what the decision owner does with an assessed candidate; a disposition consumes a core result and is not one.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:refinements-map-totally-to-core","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"relation","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:distinguishes","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:disposition-consumes-a-core-result"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:refinement","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:outer-contract","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"An outer transformation T: A → X with success predicates P₀ … Pₙ is faithfully refined by steps Tᵢ when each admitted input satisfying Pᵢ yields an output satisfying Pᵢ₊₁, retains every applicable invariant, exposes other outcomes without coercion, and each output satisfies the next step's declared domain and preconditions, as typed composition requires. Then a successful composite carries P₀ to Pₙ by induction. A refinement carries an earlier output to a later step other than the next only through a declared adapter, itself a step composed under AC-016, or a declared specialised contract, in either case one whose declared domain names what is carried; a specialised contract is declared under its owner's exact authority, context, basis, scope, preservation, loss, refusal and invalidation law.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:p4a-statement","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:support"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:nothing-is-coerced-to-success","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:faithful-refinement-definition"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:result-algebra","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:r-satisfied","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"A missing, failed or out-of-scope result returns its own member, never satisfied.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:result-algebra-has-five-members","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:forbids","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:nothing-is-coerced-to-success"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:odd-closure-decision","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"The closure decision over an edge is a sum type with a closed vocabulary: close, yield, retry, repair, re-enter, reprice, block. Each disposition is replay-visible and must carry basis and reason refs sufficient to reproduce the decision. The edge's closure decision does not select the next action: action selection belongs to evaluate_next over the closure decision plus fresh eval_gap truth. Repair and re-entry are graph actions that evaluate_next selects from admitted closure truth and published action authority, not local retry branches over strings; evaluate_action may emit repair or re-enter as a closure disposition, and evaluate_next selects which published graph action realises it. Disposition is conceptual; selection is invocational (A11).","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"ODD §11.5D A8, A11; P5, P6","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:odd-closure-decision-is-a-closed-sum-type"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:odd-closure-decision","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:refinement-profile-closure","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:result-algebra","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:target"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:r-satisfied","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:target"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:r-falsified","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:target"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:r-indeterminate","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:target"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:r-out-of-frame","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:target"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:r-invalid-basis","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:target"},{"literal":"Total mapping to the five core members, adding none (the one-algebra rule of ACTIVATION §3). Each closure decision, read with the cause or evidence its basis and reason refs record, maps to exactly one core member, which is what a composite over the edge joins; the decision keeps its own vocabulary and refs. close -> satisfied: the ledger's admitted evidence fulfils the edge's obligations on the exact basis. yield -> indeterminate: the edge stays lawful and its closure is not yet decided; it reaches indeterminate by the stop-state route of construction availability's incomplete, not as the evaluation's result, without failure classification, as A9 requires. retry -> falsified or indeterminate: falsified only when admissible evidence defeats the edge for this attempt while the same action stays lawful, otherwise indeterminate; a liveness interruption alone never yields falsified (A10); A9 separates this failure-classified re-attempt from yield. repair -> falsified or indeterminate: the result is locally defective while the governing relation stays coherent (ACTIVATION §3 Disposition, local_repair), whose defect is in the implementation or in the proof; falsified when admitted evidence shows the implementation failing an edge obligation, the failing obligation row being the counterexample; otherwise indeterminate, the defect being in the proof, so the admitted evidence cannot decide the obligation, and the decision's reason refs name the repaired proof that would decide. re-enter -> out_of_frame or invalid_basis: the edge cannot close on its current basis because an upstream asset or governing relation must change; the member follows the cause in the decision's reason refs, as construction availability maps re_entry_requested under ACTIVATION §3: out_of_frame when the cause is an undeclared relation, capability or authority, and invalid_basis for every other cause, the current basis being unable to support the edge, as when it is stale, substituted or unrepairable. reprice -> out_of_frame: further work needs a selected outcome or bound that no admitted basis declares; the decision names it, its owner and the constitutional re-entry it requests, which is the reconfiguration pressure of out_of_frame (ACTIVATION §4). block -> out_of_frame or invalid_basis: evaluate_action decides that the action just taken leaves the edge unable to proceed on its current basis; the member follows the cause in the decision's reason refs, as for re-enter.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:construction-availability-maps-to-core","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:support"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:disposition-consumes-a-core-result","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:support"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:reconfiguration-follows-the-cause","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:support"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:refinements-map-totally-to-core","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"relation","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:maps-to","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:odd-closure-decisions-map-to-core"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:odd-cumulative-environment","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:composition","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"Composition is not modelled as 'the last output feeds the next input'; the ODD law is a cumulative typed environment. Each retained GraphFunction should declare environment.requires, environment.provides and environment.carries. A later function may require any typed binding available in the cumulative carried environment, not only the immediately previous output. A product that publishes graph functions without this cumulative environment law has a line that is graph-shaped but structurally wrong.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"ODD §11.8 (mandatory); P4a, P4b, P6","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:odd-cumulative-environment-law"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:refinement","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:odd-cumulative-environment","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"ACTIVATION §4 generalises the refinement of one outer vector into an inner workflow to any realisation, lets a refinement carry an earlier output to a later step only through a declared adapter or specialised contract whose declared domain names it, and names PROFILES §2, which indexes this profile, as the keeper of the ODD binding. This profile declares the cumulative carried environment of §11.8 as that specialised contract; §11.8 is conserved as profile law and is not generalised into the core. Preserved meaning: the outer vector stays the callable contract; the inner steps conserve it and every applicable invariant; and each inner function's input satisfies its declared domain and preconditions, as AC-016 requires. Narrowed scope: one published outer vector and its declared inner workflow, whose retained functions should declare `environment.requires`, `environment.provides` and `environment.carries` (§11.8); a later function's declared domain is its `environment.requires`, which may require any typed binding available in the cumulative carried environment, not only the immediately previous output.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"ODD section 5 Graph functions, binding of refinement; P4a, P4b, P1","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:faithful-refinement-definition","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:support"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:odd-cumulative-environment-law","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:odd-graph-function-binding-declares-the-environment-contract"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:odd-negative-proof","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:odd-supported-authority-path","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"Negative proof for an ODD or graph-native boundary exercises the supported Product authority path. It must not manufacture the refusal state, blocked event, gap or verdict that the system is supposed to derive. Closure-grade negative evidence (1) identifies the supported entry and the governing authority; (2) invalidates the real authority-bearing input; (3) exercises the supported path; (4) proves refusal before the prohibited effect; and (5) establishes that no legacy, fallback, reconstruction or parallel path succeeds. Source, packaged, installed and runtime absence are distinct claims.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"ODD §11.7B, STDO-UP-010; P6, P5, P3","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:odd-negative-proof-exercises-the-real-authority-path"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:odd-supported-authority-path","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:odd-negative-proof","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"Where these identities apply, the supported relation is: public entry -> admitted GTL composition owns traversal topology -> named GraphFunction supplies the callable work contract -> implementation or plugin binding realizes only its admitted seam -> ABG owns traversal, event, continuation and replay truth -> replay-derived projection -> typed Product outcome or continuation. No CLI, SDK, service, adapter, plugin, fixture, query or projection may become a rival traversal controller. The consumer owns the concrete test and evidence mechanism; this section owns the property that mechanism must prove.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"ODD §11.7B, STDO-UP-010; P6, P4a","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:forbids","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:odd-supported-path-has-no-rival-controller"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:odd-closure-decision","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:odd-liveness","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"A9: yield is the lawful iteration boundary: the same edge or attempt remains lawful, progress or waiting state is admitted, the resume basis is replay-visible, and control returns without failure classification. Yield is not retry, not block, not timeout and not a local CLI loop; it lets long-running, bounded or partially productive work return control without losing the current edge. A10: liveness observes activity, inactivity, process state and interruption; it can support yield or a liveness interruption, and it cannot by itself declare semantic failure, semantic closure or requirement non-satisfaction.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"ODD §11.5D A9, A10; P5, P0, P6","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:distinguishes","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:odd-yield-is-lawful-iterate-not-failure"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:p0-bounded-construction","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"A finite actor realises a selected outer contract through steps; each step's selected context fits the actor's envelope; the actor's internal path within a step is its own.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:premise-selected-outcome","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:support"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:premise-actor-change","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:support"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:step-produced-facts-are-not-reacquirable","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:support"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:premise-open-world","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:support"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:premise-candidate-until-evaluated","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:support"},{"literal":"Standing: recovered as a composite; the generic statement is reframed from the graph profile's graph functions.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:p0-statement"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:p4a-typed-composition","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:composition","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"Two steps compose only when the first's result type and judgment satisfy the second's exact declared domain and preconditions; composition retains both identities, intermediate results, judgments, evidence, authority, provenance and stop states.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"Standing: independent.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:p4a-statement"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:p5-totality","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:p0-statement","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:premise"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:premise-open-world","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:premise"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:p6-statement","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:premise"},{"literal":"A step can meet a condition outside its context and cannot report success on one; its result algebra carries indeterminate, out_of_frame and invalid_basis as first-class outcomes and its control model names the next move.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:consequence"},{"literal":"Standing: derived.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"relation","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:derives","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:p5-derivation"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:p6-justification-authority","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"Definitions, assumptions, observations, candidate judgments and accepted claims have distinct standing; evidence supports a claim on a basis; authority permits or disposes within scope.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"Standing: independent. A bounded actor satisfying all else can still take a green label as acceptance.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:p6-statement"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:p0-bounded-construction","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"The actor of one step need not be the actor of the next; a later actor may re-acquire declared sources but not a prior actor's private memory.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:premise"}],"clause_type":"relation","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:premise-actor-change"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:p0-bounded-construction","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"A step's output is a candidate until evaluated.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:premise"}],"clause_type":"relation","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:premise-candidate-until-evaluated"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:p0-bounded-construction","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"The world is open: a step may meet conditions outside its selected context.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:premise"}],"clause_type":"relation","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:premise-open-world"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:p0-bounded-construction","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:outcome","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:premise"},{"literal":"P0 presupposes a selected outcome (P2).","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"relation","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:premise-selected-outcome"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:reconfiguration","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:r-out-of-frame","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:r-invalid-basis","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:r-indeterminate","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"An out_of_frame, invalid_basis, repeated indeterminate or incompatible result causes one of: supply the missing admissible evidence; select another actor inside the frame's capability envelope; activate another existing frame; refine or extend a frame declaration; revise the frame set (REFERENCE_FRAME section 10); change the evaluation; or re-enter the governing product or method relation. The disposition follows the cause; a difficult evaluation alone does not prove that another frame is required.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"P5, P2","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:diagnostic-order-is-eight-questions-in-order","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:reconfiguration-follows-the-cause"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:refinement-construction-availability","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:refinement-dispo